node_modules/
dist/
.env
.env.local
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
server/.env
server/data/

# Backups and dated copies of an env file. `server/.env` alone did not cover these, and three
# of them — each holding TUYA_ACCESS_SECRET and the Supabase service-role key — were sitting
# untracked in the Pi's checkout on 2026-08-25, one `git add -A` away from a PUBLIC repository.
# Written broadly on purpose: the next backup will be named something nobody predicted.
.env.bak*
*.env.bak*
.env.backup*
server/.env.*
# ...but the checked-in template is the whole point of having one.
!server/.env.example

# Generated baseline reports (Milestone 1 artifacts). Dated copies belong with the
# submission, not in the repository, where the wrong quarter would eventually get cited.
#
# LEADING SLASH, so this means the reports directory at the ROOT and not any directory called
# `reports` anywhere in the tree. Unanchored it also matched `src/components/reports/`, where the
# Reports page lives: the files already committed there stayed tracked, so nothing looked wrong,
# but a NEW file added beside them was silently ignored — absent from `git status`, absent from
# the commit, and gone on the next clone with no error at any point. Measured 2026-09-01 with a
# probe file and `git check-ignore`.
/reports/
